# containers.list — rootless Podman (the feature containers; `vikix containers
# setup`, or `vikix add containers`). Names checked against void-packages on
# 2026-10-16: podman 5.8.8_1 depends on runc (not crun), conmon, cni-plugins,
# slirp4netns, fuse-overlayfs, passt, netavark, containers-common,
# containers.image and containers.storage, so those are not named again.
# aardvark-dns 1.17.1 is not one of those dependencies, and netavark's DNS
# needs it. crun 1.30.1 is named on purpose: Distrobox passes --pids-limit,
# and runc refuses that when the user cannot write a cgroup. crun ignores
# that failure when it is not using systemd, and Void builds it with
# --disable-systemd. Distrobox is not in Void; the setup fetches a pinned tag.
# Podman's template installs service files and does not enable them. Vikix
# does not enable a root daemon either: rootless Podman starts nothing
# until a container runs.
podman          # rootless containers; the root services stay off
aardvark-dns    # DNS inside a container's network, which netavark runs
crun            # the runtime a box uses; runc stays, because Podman depends on it
